U.S. Bureau of Reclamation. Conduct of Power Operations, FIST 1-2, July 2012; Conduct of Power Maintenance, FIST 6-2, March 2006. [Official catalogue and complete linked manuals](https://www.usbr.gov/power/data/fist_pub.html).

Read both complete manuals for the relationship between equipment state, operating responsibility, handovers, work coordination, records, maintenance and return to service. Build a technically grounded account of how a facility remains understandable and operable across people and shifts. Link each operation to the design, limits and evidence that make it appropriate.

Catalogue identity/dates were checked on 29 October 2026. These operational practices are specific institutional technical sources; they are not a new Lince permission system or a claim that their older requirements override current law or equipment instructions. Actual documents, current revisions and component notices govern reuse. Learning from a complete facility case is distinct from being qualified to operate it. No manuals, internal procedures or operating logs are bundled.

